@title Tony Hawk's Underground (USA)
@file Tony Hawk's Underground (U).gba
@game BTOE
@chip EEPROM (EEPROM_V122; 64 Kbit, an 8 KB file on all three)
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# No save: logos and title run straight into Story mode's intro text; four
# A taps reach ENTER NAME, name "ABBA", default outfit, "Continue? YES"
# writes the battery save. Then the New Jersey story card, Benny's
# dialogue tapped through (the taps also ollie the skater into a bail),
# pause > Skater Progress > Goals, back out and skate on. [load]: the
# title opens T.H.U.G. (STORY selected, "active game abba"), STORY >
# CONTINUE GAME shows ABBA's story card and resumes at Benny's dialogue.
# Findings (recorded 2026-10-16):
# - Menus over the translucent red panel (outfit, continue_prompt, the
#   [load] menus) differ by one step in a colour channel between all
#   three: BLDCNT 0x1F41, BLDALPHA 0x0808, BG0 (31,0,0) over BG3; VRAM,
#   OAM and palette are byte-identical in the three. dingbat's pixels are
#   floor((A*8 + B*8) / 16) per channel (GBATEK) at every pixel checked
#   (e.g. (6,38): BG3 (18,25,30) -> (24,12,15)); mgba and the second
#   reference come out one higher in red at those pixels, and the second
#   reference also in blue elsewhere in the band (y 38-147), so they do
#   not agree with each other either. Compared by text.
# - The skater's shadow (a few pixels at the skater, dialogue screens) is
#   one step brighter in red/blue on the second reference alone.
# - resumed: mgba stands alone (its skater got up from the bail on another
#   frame and rode to the porch: "PRESS L TO TALK"); dingbat and the second
#   reference show the same scene.
[new]
wait 270
wait 60
wait 240
wait 60
wait 240
checkpoint title window=30
wait 240
wait 60
tap A times=4 every=40 hold=4
wait 30
press A
wait 20
press RIGHT
wait 20
press A
wait 20
press A
wait 20
press LEFT
wait 20
press A
wait 30
checkpoint name_entry window=30
press START
wait 90
checkpoint outfit window=30 compare=text
press START
wait 90
checkpoint continue_prompt window=30 compare=text
press A
wait 360
checkpoint story_card window=30
tap A times=12 every=40 hold=4
wait 120
wait 60
tap A times=6 every=40 hold=6
wait 30
tap A times=6 every=40 hold=6
wait 30
wait 120
wait 60
press START
wait 60
checkpoint paused window=30 compare=text
tap DOWN times=2 every=15 hold=4
wait 20
press A
wait 60
tap DOWN times=2 every=15 hold=4
wait 20
press A
wait 60
checkpoint goals window=30 compare=text
press B
wait 30
press B
wait 30
press B
wait 60
hold RIGHT
wait 60
release
wait 60
checkpoint resumed window=30

[load]
wait 900
checkpoint main_menu window=30 compare=text
press A
wait 90
wait 60
press A
wait 240
checkpoint continue_card window=30
tap A times=12 every=40 hold=4
wait 120
checkpoint resumed_skate window=30

